# A kernel-checked certificate: the large first-zero range

The large first-zero range (paper Theorem 12.6), generated by
`computations/graded/graded_large.py --lean-module` in the research repository: the leaf of the range `λ₁ ≥ 3/2`
(150 bins and a tail, one near row) and its certificate (36 threshold intervals).
`checkLeaf` is evaluated by the kernel (`decide +kernel`), and `certified` turns the result
into the bound `objective < S` at every feasible point.
-/

